IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `atv-seat`

-- Cases for the seat layer (atv-seat.l4): the person changing planes at a German airport.
-- Expected values are written from AufenthV § 26 and Anlage C as deposited, not from this encoding's output.
-- Case A is the traveller in the article's Case 2 "Potential exploit": a Malian national changing planes at Frankfurt between two non-Schengen countries,
-- staying in the international transit area, holding no document that already exempts her from the transit visa requirement.
-- Arguments, in order: nationality, only in the transit area, holds a transit visa, exempt under Art. 3(5), Annex IV state,
-- visa and ticket for AU IL NZ, returning to Jordan, onward flight within twelve hours, official passport (and, where asked, an exception applies).

§ `Case A: a Malian national in transit at Frankfurt, no exempting document`

-- As Annex C is printed on 2026-11-02, Mali is listed: she must hold the visa.
#ASSERT `must I hold an airport transit visa under Annex C as printed` "Mali" TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Without the visa she is not exempt from the residence-title requirement while she waits in the transit area (§ 26(2) sentence 2).
#ASSERT NOT (`am I exempt from the residence title requirement in transit under Annex C as printed` "Mali" TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- If the 2015 addition of Mali is void for want of citation and no exception is accepted, she needs no visa through Annex C ...
#ASSERT NOT (`must I hold an airport transit visa if the 2015 additions are void` "Mali" TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- ... and § 26(1) then exempts her from the residence-title requirement without one.
#ASSERT `am I exempt from the residence title requirement in transit if the 2015 additions are void` "Mali" TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The article's follow-up on the earlier-citation exception: if a court accepted one, the additions stand and the visa is required.
#ASSERT `must I hold an airport transit visa if the 2015 additions are void` "Mali" TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- The fact the whole case turns on: the article's quotation of the 2015 preamble does not name § 99(3a) AufenthG.
#ASSERT NOT (`does the 2015 preamble cite the power to add a state to Annex C`)

§ `Case B: the same Malian national, holding a residence permit of an EU state`

-- She is within an Art. 3(5) category (asked as a fact): no visa under either reading.
#ASSERT NOT (`must I hold an airport transit visa under Annex C as printed` "Mali" TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`must I hold an airport transit visa if the 2015 additions are void` "Mali" TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Case C: a Jordanian national flying on to Sydney`

-- Anlage C, Jordanien (a): visa and ticket for Australia and an onward flight within twelve hours: exempt, whichever reading.
#ASSERT NOT (`must I hold an airport transit visa under Annex C as printed` "Jordan" TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- The same traveller whose onward flight leaves after thirteen hours is not exempt.
#ASSERT `must I hold an airport transit visa under Annex C as printed` "Jordan" TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Case D: a South Sudanese national, the other entry the 2015 regulation added`

#ASSERT `must I hold an airport transit visa under Annex C as printed` "South Sudan" TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`must I hold an airport transit visa if the 2015 additions are void` "South Sudan" TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
